 3. Activities Performed
3.1 Footprinting and Reconnaissance
I performed authorized reconnaissance on the networkwalks.com domain using six Kali Linux tools.
Each tool provided different information about the website and its infrastructure.
Step 1: WHOIS
I started with WHOIS to collect publicly available domain registration information.
It helped me understand basic information about the domain and identify its name servers.
Step 2: WhatWeb
I used WhatWeb to identify the technologies used by the website.
The results identified:
- WordPress 7.0.4- WP Download Manager 3.3.58- Other technical information related to the website
This information can help a security professional understand what technologies may need to be reviewed during authorized testing.
Step 3: Nslookup
I used Nslookup to resolve the domain name and find its associated IP address.
The observed IP address was:
192.232.216.135
Step 4: Curl
I used the following command to check the HTTP response headers:
curl -I networkwalks.com
The response provided additional information about the web application.
It also showed the WordPress REST API endpoint:
/wp-json/
Step 5: Wafw00f
I used Wafw00f to check whether a Web Application Firewall was being used.
The result identified:
ModSecurity (SpiderLabs)
This showed that the website uses a WAF as part of its security setup.
Step 6: DNSRecon
Finally, I used DNSRecon to collect publicly available DNS information.
The results included information about:
- Name servers- Mail servers- SPF/TXT records- Service records- DNS software
This helped me understand how DNS information can provide additional details about an organization's infrastructure.
