 3.2 Network Scanning with Zenmap
The second activity involved scanning my own local network using Zenmap.
The purpose was to:
- Identify my local IP address.- Identify the network subnet.- Find active devices.- Identify IP addresses.- Identify MAC addresses.- Create a network topology.
Step 1: Find the Local Network
I used the Windows "ipconfig" command to check my local IP address and network information.
The subnet was then entered into Zenmap.
Step 2: Perform a Ping Scan
I used Zenmap's Ping Scan option to identify active devices on the authorized local network.
The practical example showed the following live hosts:
192.168.10.112192.168.10.109192.168.10.109
The example also showed three MAC addresses.
