 5. Recommendations
Based on the findings from the exercises, I recommend the following:
1. Review Publicly Available Information
Organizations should regularly check what information about their websites, technologies, CMS platforms, and plugins is publicly visible.
2. Keep Software Updated
CMS platforms, plugins, and other web technologies should be regularly updated and checked against current security advisories.
3. Review HTTP Headers
HTTP response headers should be reviewed to make sure unnecessary technical information is not being exposed.
4. Review DNS Records
DNS records should be checked regularly to make sure only necessary information and services are publicly available.
5. Configure and Monitor the WAF
The Web Application Firewall, such as ModSecurity, should remain enabled and properly configured.
It should also be monitored and updated when necessary.
6. Perform Regular Network Discovery
Organizations should regularly scan their own internal networks to identify active devices.
7. Investigate Unknown Devices
Any unexpected device found during a network scan should be investigated and verified.
8. Keep Network Documentation Updated
Network diagrams and device information should be documented and updated regularly.
9. Always Get Authorization
Reconnaissance and scanning should only be performed on systems and networks where proper authorization has been provided.
